      "text": "Puerto Madryn and the Valdés Peninsula"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8e829c22e916bd5ad9a9e09e47f1964f64a1390e88e7606023c5249a5ecea814",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "submit-9e9cff89-eaf8-4da3-b719-163cca50324d-01",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, set out early for the Valdés Peninsula on the Atlantic coast of Chubut Province.\n\nThe peninsula covers 3,625 square kilometres and has several salt lakes. It has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1999.\n\nThe peninsula is home to a wide range of wildlife, including elephant seals, sea lions, seals, fur seals and penguins.\n\nSouthern right whales come into Golfo Nuevo. You’ll set out by boat from Puerto Pirámides to look for them. The whales come fairly close to shore, and you may see them in their natural habitat during the boat trip.\n\nThe boat trip takes about 1.5 hours.\n\nAfter the boat trip, continue to the San Lorenzo reserve for lunch and a walk among Magellanic penguins.\n\nReturn to Puerto Madryn.\n\n**Meals:** breakfast."
    },
